# Applications workstream

This chat/session owns **Short-term applications** in the monday CRM portal.

## Repo

- Work in this repo only: `Documents/Monday/monday`
- Do not touch `crm-prototype` unless the user explicitly asks

## Scope (you own)

- Short-term applications pipeline list and detail
- Pipeline sections, filters, status display, term notes chat
- Read-only UX guards (disable writes when view-only)
- Column mapping: `columnMap.ts`, `timelineMap.ts`
- Application-specific hooks: `useApplication*.ts`, `useApplicationsPipeline.ts`

## Active plan

Follow `.cursor/plans/short-term_applications_view_b69059c7.plan.md`:

- In progress: `resolve-board-id` — use `resolveApplicationsBoardId` in `useApplicationsPipeline`
- Pending: column discovery, read-only UI, list shell parity with Contacts, detail verify, cross-nav verify, build verify

## Environment

- `VITE_APPLICATIONS_BOARD_ID` — required for live pipeline
- `VITE_APPLICATION_NOTES_WRITABLE` — keep **off** for view-only phase
- Future: `VITE_APPLICATIONS_WRITABLE`
- Shared: `VITE_MONDAY_READ_ONLY`, `VITE_MONDAY_API_PROXY_URL`

## Out of scope (do not touch unless task explicitly requires it)

- Contacts list, detail, profile edit, tags, internal notes
- `ContactsPage`, `contactsApi.ts`, `contactMap.ts`, contact components
- Exception: cross-nav verification (Contacts → application focus) may read Contacts nav props in `Dashboard.tsx`

## Shared files — minimal diffs only

When editing shared infrastructure, change only Applications-related code:

| File | Applications-owned areas |
|------|-------------------------|
| `src/config/boards.ts` | `canEditApplications()`, `resolveApplicationsBoardId()` |
| `src/services/crmApi.ts` | `fetchApplicationsPipeline`, status/notes mutations |
| `src/pages/Dashboard.tsx` | `applicationFocusId` / focus behavior |
| `.env.example` | applications vars section |

Do not change Contacts write flags or `resolveContactsBoardId()` without user approval.

## Dev servers

- `npm run dev` (port 4040)
- `npm run monday:proxy` for live monday API
